# "If a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard this card, put it onto the battlefield instead of putting it
# into your graveyard." Bot2 begins with Leyline of the Void ("If a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere,
# exile it instead"), so when Bot2's Liliana of the Veil makes Bot1 discard a Wilt-Leaf Liege both replacements would change the
# discard, and Bot1, the affected card's owner, chooses which applies (CR 616.1, 616.1e; the Liege's 2024-11-08 ruling). On turn 6
# Bot1 takes the Liege's: it is put onto the battlefield, and the Leyline then no longer applies (CR 616.1f). On turn 8 Bot1 takes
# the Leyline's for its second Liege: it is exiled, so the Liege's own replacement, which only replaces going to the graveyard, no
# longer applies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Wilt-Leaf Liege x2
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Leyline of the Void
Swamp x3
Liliana of the Veil
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot2.Accept
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp#3.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Liliana of the Veil.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Activate(Ability: Each player)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Wilt-Leaf Liege)
Bot1.Replace(Wilt-Leaf Liege)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
? Exile.Count = 0
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T8 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Activate(Ability: Each player)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Wilt-Leaf Liege)
Bot1.Replace(Leyline of the Void)

[Expect]
Turn = 8
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Island; Wilt-Leaf Liege; Island
Exile = Wilt-Leaf Liege
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Swamp; Swamp
